// Local.xcconfig.example — template for machine-local build settings.
//
// Retain is a public repository, so no development team is stored in
// Retain.xcodeproj. Unsigned local builds need none. Signing a build for
// distribution does, and picking a team in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities
// editor writes it straight back into project.pbxproj — where it would be
// committed and public.
//
// So the team lives here instead: copy this file to Local.xcconfig and put your
// own Team ID in. Base.xcconfig, which the project uses as its base
// configuration, includes it optionally, so a clone without it still builds.
// Local.xcconfig is in .gitignore and never reaches a commit.
//
// Your Team ID is the ten-character string in the Membership tab of your Apple
// Developer account.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
